# SABOTAGE: the HOST half of Pages search — `Samenerp.Seeds.seed_notes_pages!/1` registers the
# block-search index after it seeds the demo page. Mounting the surface is not making it
# searchable: `Samen.Web.Notes.Search` is fail-closed, so with no registry rows `/pages?q=` renders
# the honest empty state and every other test in the host still passes. This patch deletes the ONE
# registration call and nothing else, so the only thing that can fail is the test that asserts a
# seeded page is actually found by its plain block text.
#
# What it refutes is the claim that registration is wired on the seed path at all (the alternative
# reading of the old code — "the mount is in the router, so search must work" — is exactly the
# confusion this pins). The registry rows themselves are still written by the direct
# `Seeds.ensure_notes_search_index!/1` test, which is why the sabotage targets the SEED call rather
# than the registration function: dropping the function would fail two tests and tell us less.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: the guard (`Samen.Scopes.Primitives.SearchIndexGuard`), the vaulted
# block seed, and `search/4` — this removes a REGISTRATION, not the PII refusal or the engine.
#
# No warning is introduced: `ensure_notes_search_index!/1` stays used by `seed!/0,1`, so nothing is
# left unused and no warning needs confining.
# APP: samenerp
# TEST_FILES: test/notes_search_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a seeded page is found by its PLAIN block text through the real /pages?q=
--- a/samenerp/lib/samenerp/seeds.ex
+++ b/samenerp/lib/samenerp/seeds.ex
@@ -154,6 +154,5 @@
         })
     end
 
-    :ok = ensure_notes_search_index!(org_id)
 
     doc.id
   end
